                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Psalm 123 Reliance on the Lord - A song of ascents. To you I raise my eyes, to you enthroned in heaven.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "2",
                       "number":  2,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Yes, like the eyes of servants on the hand of their masters, Like the eyes of a maid on the hand of her mistress, So our eyes are on the LORD our God, till we are shown favor.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "3",
                       "number":  3,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Show us favor, LORD, show us favor, for we have our fill of contempt.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   },
                   {
                       "label":  "4",
                       "number":  4,
                       "subVerseIndex":  0,
                       "paragraphNumber":  0,
                       "paragraphIndex":  0,
                       "text":  "Our souls are more than sated with mockery from the insolent, with contempt from the arrogant.",
                       "isPoetry":  false
                   }
               ],
    "marks":  [

              ]
}